  "description": "Addition of third floor to create 3nos flats comprising 2nos 2bed flats and 1no 1bed flat.",
  "epc_number": null,
  "ward": "Kingston Town",
  "last_updated": "2026-11-27T18:03:35.218Z",
  "street_name": "Mill Place",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development fails to comply with the statutory requirements of Section 3(9A) and Condition AA.1(f) of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended), in that Flat 11 fails to achieve the minimum gross internal floor area of 50 square metres required by the nationally described space standard for a one-bedroom, two-person dwelling, and the applicant has failed to provide section drawings to demonstrate that the internal floor-to-ceiling height of the additional storey complies with the height limitations set out in the Order.",
    "The proposed upward extension, by virtue of its scale, height, and overall massing, would result in a top-heavy addition that disrupts the architectural proportions of the host building, erodes the visual subservience of the roofscape, and appears incongruous and excessively dominant within the streetscene, resulting in unacceptable harm to the external appearance of the building having regard to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework and Condition AA.2(1)(e) of Schedule 2, Part 20, Class AA of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The applicant has failed to provide a daylight and sunlight assessment, sufficient survey and plan information identifying neighbouring sensitive windows and private external amenity areas, or a noise impact assessment to evaluate potential noise impacts from nearby commercial premises (including the nearby MOT garage). Consequently, insufficient information has been submitted to demonstrate that the proposed development would safeguard the residential amenity and living conditions of neighbouring and intended occupiers with regard to daylight, sunlight, privacy, outlook, and noise, contrary to Conditions AA.2(1)(g) and AA.2(1)(h) and paragraph B(3)(b) of Schedule 2, Part 20 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) and the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
